# The L0 golden corpus: the BYTES ARE THE EVIDENCE.
#
# These files are compared byte for byte by tests/program/test_l0_corpus, so git must never
# transform them on checkout. Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites every LF as CRLF and
# the byte-stability check fails there while passing on Linux -- which is exactly what
# happened in CI on #299: three builds red on a corpus that was green locally.
#
# A golden corpus whose bytes depend on the platform that checked it out is not golden.
*.l0 -text

# Deployment spec fixtures, for the same reason: test_deployment_spec compares the canonical
# JSON byte for byte, so a CRLF rewrite on a Windows checkout would fail there and nowhere
# else. Verified by converting the fixture and watching exactly that assertion break.
#
# Scoped to the fixture directory rather than all *.json: generated traces and tool output
# are not evidence and have no reason to be pinned.
tests/program/deploy/*.json -text
